-- title:
--   Torus–compact coordinates for the zeroth shell of GL₃(A_ℚ)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ (the group `AdelicGL 3 (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ`) characterised by `hK`: an element $k$ lies in $K$ exactly when its archimedean component satisfies $k^{\mathsf T}k=1$ over the infinite adeles, and for every height-one prime $p$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ its component at $p$ has all entries, and all entries of its inverse, of valuation at most $1$. Equip $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ and the idele group with their Borel $\sigma$-algebras. Then for every Haar measure $\kappa$ on $K$ there is a constant $c\in[0,\infty]$ with $c\neq 0$ and $c\neq\infty$ such that for every measurable $F:\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})\to[0,\infty]$ satisfying $F(ng)=F(g)$ for all $g$ and all $n$ in the subgroup generated by the upper unipotent matrices `upperUnipotent3 x y z` with adelic entries, the integral of $q\mapsto F(q.\mathrm{out})$ over [`WhittakerBlock.zerothShell ∅`](def/LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_WhittakerBlock.html#L34) — the set of orbits $q$ whose component at every finite $p$ factors as an upper unipotent matrix times an element of the local maximal compact — against the quotient measure obtained from the adelic Haar measure of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ and the Haar measure of the unipotent subgroup, equals $c$ times $\int\!\!\int F(\mathrm{diag}(t_0,t_1,t_2)k)\,\|t_0\|^{-2}\|t_2\|^{2}\,d\kappa(k)\,dt$, where $\|\cdot\|$ is the idele norm given by the module of the adelic Haar character and $t$ ranges over triples of ideles against the threefold product of [`NumberField.Idele.sPartMeasure ℚ ∅`](def/NumberField_IdeleProductMeasure.html#L458), the pushforward to the component at infinity of the idelic Haar measure restricted to the ideles that are units at all finite primes.
--
--   This is the Iwasawa-type change of variables for the zeroth shell of $N(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})\backslash\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$: integration over the shell is rewritten as an integral over the diagonal torus and the maximal compact, the factor $\|t_0\|^{-2}\|t_2\|^{2}$ being the inverse modulus of the Borel subgroup on the diagonal. It is used in the estimate of the Whittaker block on the empty set of primes that enters the construction of a cubic automorphic induction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_WhittakerBlock_setLIntegral_zerothShell_eq_mul_lintegral_torus.lean

